NNAAMMEE
     cclleeaann--oolldd--ddiissttffiilleess — remove obsolete ports distfiles

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     cclleeaann--oolldd--ddiissttffiilleess [--mmnnvvxx] [--ee _e_x_c_e_p_t] [--hh _h_i_s_t_o_r_y] [_t_i_m_e_s_t_a_m_p]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Each time dpb(1) is run for a full scan of the ports(7) tree, it appends
     to the _h_i_s_t_o_r_y log, listing files in the _d_i_s_t_f_i_l_e_s directory that are
     not, or no longer, needed for building the complete tree.  It can also be
     run solely for that purpose, by using:

           $ ddppbb --DD HHIISSTTOORRYY__OONNLLYY

     When cclleeaann--oolldd--ddiissttffiilleess is run later, it uses the information from the
     history log to delete unneeded files.  When a file is deleted, the corre‐
     sponding entry is also deleted from the history log.

     By default, cclleeaann--oolldd--ddiissttffiilleess deletes all files listed in the history
     log.

     If a _t_i_m_e_s_t_a_m_p is given, it is interpreted as a number of seconds since
     the Epoch, similar to the date(1) --rr argument, and only those files are
     deleted that were recorded as obsolete at that time or earlier.  It can
     also be set to a date in ISO8601 format, like ‘2023-07-01’ or
     ‘2023-07-02T12:00:00Z’.

     For normal files, cclleeaann--oolldd--ddiissttffiilleess verifies sha256(1) checksums prior
     to removal.  It also removes links under _b_y___c_i_p_h_e_r_/_s_h_a_2_5_6, but it trusts
     that the checksums for these are accurate.

     Options are as follows:

     --ee _e_x_c_e_p_t
           Read exception list from file _e_x_c_e_p_t.  Each line is the name of a
           file that shouldn't be removed.

     --hh _h_i_s_t_o_r_y
           Read log from history file _h_i_s_t_o_r_y instead of the default
           _/_u_s_r_/_p_o_r_t_s_/_d_i_s_t_f_i_l_e_s_/_h_i_s_t_o_r_y.  Turns on --nnvv, as this is a testing
           option.

     --mm    Causes cclleeaann--oolldd--ddiissttffiilleess to display the progress meter even if
           not on a terminal.

     --nn    Don't really remove files.

     --vv    Display what will be removed, as ‘rm file’ lines.

     --xx    Causes cclleeaann--oolldd--ddiissttffiilleess to not display the progress meter.

FFIILLEESS
     /usr/ports  base of the ports tree, can be overridden with env variable
                 PORTSDIR.

     /usr/ports/distfiles
                 location of the distfiles repository, can be overridden with
                 env variable DISTDIR.

     /usr/ports/distfiles/history
                 log of obsolete distfiles.

